From f9f77cdadca04aa38237f5e04bb32646411eadc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 00:24:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): prebuild the seeded route-smoke DB; harden
 health-monitor step outputs

Two independent CI defects, both found while pricing the suite OOM.

1. .github/workflows/ci.yml + scripts/ci_build_smoke_db.py

instance/ is gitignored, so on a fresh CI checkout tests/test_route_smoke.py
takes its "no real DB" branch and replays the entire alembic chain once per
parametrized route, 245 times in a single process.

Measured on this tree, same machine, same 60 tests, only the presence of
instance/proam.db differing:

    seeded    peak RSS  310 MB   RC=0
    unseeded  peak RSS 1367 MB   RC=0

Full file, seeded: 245 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, 7 skipped, 52s,
peak RSS 934 MB. Unseeded extrapolates to ~5.1 GB from a four-point stair
(20/60/100/130 tests), which is the OOM.

The per-test alembic chain is 17.08 MB/test, 84% of the growth. The residual
3.26 MB/test is create_app() itself and leaks on every machine including a
developer's. Seeding makes the leak survivable, not absent.

A bare `flask db upgrade` is NOT sufficient. The use_real_db branch skips
_seed_minimal_smoke_data entirely and the fixture then does

    ids["tournament_id"] = first_tournament.id

with no None guard, so a migrated-but-unseeded file would AttributeError on
all 245 tests. The script therefore migrates AND seeds, reusing the test
module's own seeding function rather than a second copy that could drift,
and asserts all eleven required entities exist before exiting 0.

Caveat, stated rather than buried: `Run tests` still passes -x, and ten
pre-existing failures (nine in tests/test_mark_assignment.py, one in
tests/test_identity_migration.py) abort the run before test_route_smoke is
reached. This change is what stops the job OOMing the moment those are
fixed or -x is dropped; it does not by itself turn CI green.

2. .github/workflows/health-monitor.yml

The step wrote its multiline `body` output using the fixed, publicly readable
heredoc delimiter HEALTH_EOF, and wrote four single-line outputs straight
from `jq -r` on the same untrusted response body.

Reproduced with a body containing a literal HEALTH_EOF line and a .status
string carrying embedded newlines, then parsed the way the runner parses
$GITHUB_OUTPUT:

    before: injected_via_delim=yes and injected_via_singleline=yes both
            appear as step outputs, plus an orphan trailing HEALTH_EOF line
    after:  neither key exists; status collapses to one harmless value

Fix is GitHub's documented practice: a per-run random delimiter, plus
newline stripping and a length cap on every value derived from the body.

Severity, honestly: this is output injection, not code execution. An earlier
report from this audit called the heredoc at line 99 a live RCE path via
command substitution on $BODY_RAW. That was wrong. Bash does not re-scan the
result of a parameter expansion for command substitution; a payload of
$(touch /tmp/PWNED) inside the body was emitted literally and created
nothing. That claim is retracted. Reachability of the real defect is also
low: /health is generated by this app from internal state, not from
attacker-controlled input.

Verification: ruff clean, both workflows parse as YAML, the rendered
health-monitor step passes bash -n, /tmp/proam rig unchanged at 343cb92.
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml             |  11 +++
 .github/workflows/health-monitor.yml |  24 ++++--
 scripts/ci_build_smoke_db.py         | 112 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 141 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 scripts/ci_build_smoke_db.py

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index f7f14f5..2bbec10 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -30,6 +30,17 @@ jobs:
           pip install -r requirements.txt
           pip install pytest
 
+      # instance/ is gitignored, so on a fresh checkout tests/test_route_smoke.py
+      # takes its "no real DB" branch and replays the entire alembic chain once
+      # per parametrized route — 245 times in one process. That leaks ~20 MB per
+      # test and peaks near 5 GB, which is what has been OOM-killing this job.
+      # Building the file once here drops the whole run to a measured 934 MB.
+      # The script migrates AND seeds: a migrate-only database makes the fixture
+      # AttributeError on first_tournament.id for all 245 tests. Sets its own
+      # DATABASE_URL/SECRET_KEY, so it needs no env block here.
+      - name: Build seeded route-smoke database
+        run: python scripts/ci_build_smoke_db.py
+
       - name: Run tests
         env:
           FLASK_ENV: testing
diff --git a/.github/workflows/health-monitor.yml b/.github/workflows/health-monitor.yml
index 648678b..0fdfb2e 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/health-monitor.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/health-monitor.yml
@@ -48,10 +48,17 @@ jobs:
           echo "HTTP code: $CODE"
           echo "Body: $BODY"
 
-          STATUS=$(echo "$BODY" | jq -r '.status // "missing"')
-          DB=$(echo "$BODY" | jq -r '.db // "missing"')
-          MIG_REV=$(echo "$BODY" | jq -r '.migration_rev // "missing"')
-          MIG_CURRENT=$(echo "$BODY" | jq -r '.migration_current // "missing"')
+          # Every value below is parsed out of an HTTP response body. The runner
+          # parses $GITHUB_OUTPUT as newline-delimited key=value, so a value
+          # carrying an embedded newline forges additional step outputs. jq -r
+          # emits real newlines for a JSON string containing \n, so strip them,
+          # and cap the length so one field cannot fill the output file.
+          jqs() { echo "$BODY" | jq -r "$1" | tr -d '\r\n' | head -c 200; }
+
+          STATUS=$(jqs '.status // "missing"')
+          DB=$(jqs '.db // "missing"')
+          MIG_REV=$(jqs '.migration_rev // "missing"')
+          MIG_CURRENT=$(jqs '.migration_current // "missing"')
 
           {
             echo "http_code=$CODE"
@@ -61,10 +68,15 @@ jobs:
             echo "migration_current=$MIG_CURRENT"
           } >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
 
+          # Per-run random heredoc delimiter, per GitHub's documented practice.
+          # A fixed, publicly-readable delimiter lets a body containing that
+          # literal line close the block early and append forged outputs, plus
+          # an orphan terminator that breaks the step.
+          DELIM="HEALTH_EOF_$(openssl rand -hex 16)"
           {
-            echo "body<<HEALTH_EOF"
+            echo "body<<$DELIM"
             echo "$BODY"
-            echo "HEALTH_EOF"
+            echo "$DELIM"
           } >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
 
           if [ "$CODE" != "200" ] || [ "$STATUS" != "ok" ] || [ "$DB" != "true" ] || [ "$MIG_CURRENT" != "true" ]; then
diff --git a/scripts/ci_build_smoke_db.py b/scripts/ci_build_smoke_db.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d4e14ec
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/ci_build_smoke_db.py
@@ -0,0 +1,112 @@
+"""Build the seeded SQLite database that tests/test_route_smoke.py expects.
+
+Why this exists
+---------------
+`smoke_env` in tests/test_route_smoke.py has two branches:
+
+    use_real_db = SOURCE_DB.exists()          # instance/proam.db
+    if use_real_db:
+        shutil.copy2(SOURCE_DB, db_copy)      # cheap
+    ...
+    if not use_real_db:
+        upgrade(directory=str(migrations_dir))  # <-- runs the WHOLE alembic
+        _seed_minimal_smoke_data(app)           #     chain, per test
+
+`instance/` is gitignored, so on a fresh CI checkout the file is absent and
+CI takes the second branch for all 245 parametrized route tests. Replaying
+the full migration chain 245 times inside one process leaks roughly
+17 MB per test on top of the ~3.3 MB per test that `create_app()` costs on
+its own. Measured stair, same machine, same suite:
+
+    tests   unseeded   seeded
+       20     554 MB    179 MB
+       60    1367 MB    310 MB
+      100    2181 MB    442 MB
+      130    2789 MB    537 MB
+      245   ~5130 MB    934 MB   (extrapolated / measured, RC=0)
+
+Roughly 20.3 MB/test unseeded against 3.3 MB/test seeded: the alembic chain
+is 84% of the growth. Building the database ONCE here and letting every test
+take the `shutil.copy2` branch is what keeps the job inside the runner's
+7 GB.
+
+A bare `flask db upgrade` is NOT sufficient. The `use_real_db` branch skips
+`_seed_minimal_smoke_data` entirely, and the fixture immediately does
+
+    ids["tournament_id"] = first_tournament.id
+
+with no None guard. A migrated-but-unseeded file would AttributeError on all
+245 tests. So this script migrates AND seeds, reusing the test module's own
+seeding function rather than a second copy of it that could drift.
+
+Run from the repository root:
+
+    python scripts/ci_build_smoke_db.py
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import os
+import sys
+from pathlib import Path
+
+PROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
+if str(PROJECT_ROOT) not in sys.path:
+    sys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_ROOT))
+
+TARGET = PROJECT_ROOT / "instance" / "proam.db"
+
+
+def main() -> int:
+    TARGET.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    if TARGET.exists():
+        TARGET.unlink()
+
+    # Set before importing app/tests: create_app() reads these at call time,
+    # but the test module runs _discover_routes() at import time.
+    os.environ["DATABASE_URL"] = f"sqlite:///{TARGET}"
+    os.environ["SECRET_KEY"] = "route-smoke-secret"
+    os.environ["FLASK_ENV"] = "testing"
+    os.environ["TESTING"] = "1"
+    # Explicitly off. This script migrates on purpose; create_all would
+    # produce a schema alembic has never stamped.
+    os.environ.pop("TEST_USE_CREATE_ALL", None)
+
+    from flask_migrate import upgrade
+
+    from app import create_app
+    from tests.test_route_smoke import _seed_minimal_smoke_data
+
+    app = create_app()
+    with app.app_context():
+        upgrade(directory=str(PROJECT_ROOT / "migrations"))
+    _seed_minimal_smoke_data(app)
+
+    # Fail loudly here rather than as 245 AttributeErrors later.
+    with app.app_context():
+        from models import Event, EventResult, Heat, Team, Tournament, User
+        from models.competitor import CollegeCompetitor, ProCompetitor
+
+        required = {
+            "tournament": Tournament.query.first(),
+            "event": Event.query.first(),
+            "heat": Heat.query.first(),
+            "user": User.query.first(),
+            "team": Team.query.first(),
+            "college_competitor": CollegeCompetitor.query.first(),
+            "pro_competitor": ProCompetitor.query.first(),
+            "event_result": EventResult.query.first(),
+            "birling_event": Event.query.filter_by(stand_type="birling").first(),
+            "partnered_event": Event.query.filter_by(is_partnered=True).first(),
+            "relay_event": Event.query.filter_by(name="Pro-Am Relay").first(),
+        }
+        missing = sorted(k for k, v in required.items() if v is None)
+        if missing:
+            print(f"FAIL: seeded database is missing: {', '.join(missing)}")
+            return 1
+
+    print(f"OK: built {TARGET} ({TARGET.stat().st_size} bytes)")
+    return 0
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    raise SystemExit(main())
-- 
2.43.0

